senses.gloss:
शंस, अस्, m., Ved. recitation, invocation; praise,
prayer, (Sāy. = स्तुति); wishing well or ill to; a
spell (for good or evil); a blessing; a curse;
calumny; = नराशंस (Ved.); (आ), f. speech;
praise, flattery, eulogium; wish, desire; (अस्, आ, अम्),
reciting; praising; wishing; [cf. दुः-श्˚.]

शंव, अस्, आ, अम्, fortunate, prosperous; happy;
(अस्), m. the thunderbolt of Indra; the iron head of
a pestle; [cf. शम्ब.]

शांशप शांशप, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. शिंशपा with
substitution of आ for इ), made of Śiṃśapā wood, &c.;
(अस्), m. a kind of cup or ladle made of Śiṃśapā wood;
a proper N.

सं-यम्य, ind. having restrained or controlled;
having bound together or fastened up; having
fastened or closed.

सं-राजत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, reigning universally;
(अन्), m. a sovereign lord (= सम्-राज्, and written
with म् in Ṛg-veda I. 27, 1).

संराध् सं-राध्, cl. 4. P. A. -राध्यति, -ते,
&c. (see rt. राध्, p. 842), to be accomplished or
perfected; to be acquired or brought into possession:
Caus. -राधयति, -यितुम्, to bring into harmony;
to agree together, agree about or upon (with loc.);
to conciliate, propitiate, appease, satisfy.

संवप् सं-वप्, cl. 1. P. A. -वपति, -ते,
-वप्तुम्, to throw together, mix, pour in, put in;
to scatter, sow.

सं-विधाय, ind. having disposed or arranged, hav-
ing appointed or fixed; having directed or ordered;
having performed; having used or employed, &c.

सं-वीक्षण, अम्, n. looking about in all direc-
tions, looking for (anything lost), search, inquiry;
looking or gazing attentively.

सं-व्यान, अम्, n. the act of covering over, a
covering; cloth, clothes, garment, vestment, vesture;
an upper garment.

सं-शुद्धि, इस्, f. thorough purification; cleansing
or cleaning (the body); purity, cleanness; clearance;
acquittal, acquittance; correction, rectification.

संस्-कर्तृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who makes perfect
or polishes, one who prepares or dresses or cooks;
one who consecrates, &c.

संस्तम्भ् सं-स्तम्भ्, cl. 5. 9. P. -स्तभ्-
नोति, -स्तभ्नाति, -स्तब्धुम्, to support, prop up;
to confirm, establish, corroborate; to stop, restrain:
Caus. -स्तम्भयति, -यितुम्, to prop up, stay, sup-
port; to confirm, strengthen, encourage; to stop;
to make immovable or rigid, stupefy, paralyze.

सं-स्तम्भ, अस्, m. support, supporting, prop;
confirming, establishing, fixing, making firm; stop,
stay; paralysis, muscular rigidity.

सं-स्तुत, अस्, आ, अम्, praised or hymned together;
praised well or properly; lauded, hymned, eulogized;
agreeing together, intimate, acquainted, known.
—संस्तुत-प्राय, अस्, आ, अम्, for the most part
lauded or hymned together, usually associated in
hymns.

सांहित सांहित, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. संहिता), re-
lating to the Saṃhitā, found in the Saṃhitā text;
(ई), f., N. of an Upaniṣad (= तैत्तिरीयोपनिषद्).

सं-हार्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be drawn together or
contracted, to be abridged; to be destroyed, &c.;
to be restrained or curbed or suppressed.

सं-हृति, इस्, f. contraction, compression, abridge-
ment; destruction, loss, disappearance; collection;
restraint; taking, seizure.

सनिष्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. desiring to bestow;
wishing for riches, desirous of wealth, (Sāy. = धनम्
इच्छत् or लप्स्यमान, Ṛg-veda VII. 100, 1.)

सन्-तति, इस्, f. stretching or extending along,
stretching or spreading over, extent, expanse, con-
tinuity; a continuous line, row, range; uninterrupted
succession, descent; lineage, race, progeny, offspring;
a son; a daughter; a number of people, multitude;
(इस्), m., N. of a son of Alarka.

सन्-तमस, अस्, आ, अम्, darkened, clouded;
(अम्), n. overspreading or universal darkness; great
darkness or delusion of mind.

सन्-देष्टव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be pointed out or
indicated, to be enjoined; to be communicated;
(अम्), n. an injunction, direction, order.

सन्-दुष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, polluted, defiled, unclean;
very depraved, wicked, bad; ill-disposed, ill-affected
towards (with gen.).

सन्-दृब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, strung together, inter-
woven, bound or collected into a tuft or bunch;
arranged, composed.

सन्धानिन्, ई, इनी, इ, tying or binding together;
clever in taking aim, shrewd; (इनी), f. a cow-house
(= गो-गृह).

सन्-ध्यातृ, ता, त्री, तृ, one who reflects or
thinks about; one who binds, (Manu VIII. 342;
probably for सन्-दातृ.)

सन्निकाश् सन्-नि-काश् (सम्-), Caus. -काश-
यति, -यितुम्, to make quite clear, manifest, reveal;
to make known, announce.

सन्निभ सन्-निभ, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. भा
with नि and सम्), like, similar, resembling, (at the
end of comps., e. g. मेघ-स्˚, resembling a cloud.)

सन्-निविष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, entered together, met
together, assembled, collected; entered deeply into;
absorbed or engrossed in; stationed in, abiding in,
resting in; inserted in, sticking in, depending on;
stationed near, contiguous, neighbouring, near, pre-
sent, at hand; seated, encamped.

सन्-निवृत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, turned back, come back,
returned, coming back; desisted, stopped, ceased;
ceasing, forbearing; withdrawing. shrinking from.

सांवादिक सांवादिक, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. सं-
वाद), colloquial, controversial, causing discussion;
(अस्), m. a disputant, controversialist, logician.

सानुक्रोश सानुक्रोश (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्,
full of compassion, compassionate, tender, kind;
(अम्), ind. compassionately, affectionately.

सान्तराल (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, having an in-
terval, separated by intervals, distinct from, apart;
together with the intermediate or mixed (castes;
see Manu II. 18).

सान्वय सान्वय (स-अन्˚), अस्, आ, अम्, along
with family or descendants; with all the race or family;
in regular order or succession; related to, of kin to.
